AB  - Background: Lung cancer is the leading cause of death of all tumors in China. Due to imbalanced development of different provinces, the surgical treatments of NSCLC in different areas of China diverse. The Chinese National NSCLC outcome registry was founded in 2013, which covers 17 provinces across China. We analyze the data of 5060 NSCLC patients retrieved from this registry to reveal the imbalanced circumstances. Methods: Data of 5060 stage I-III patients during 2013-2014 were obtained from the registry . Baseline data, surgical treatment pattern parameters, pathology, number of lymph nodes dissected, and total hospital costs were analyzed. Results: Among the patients, the mean age was 59.7 , while 3204 were male. Mean pre-op forced expiratory volume in 1 second (FEV1) was 2.23L, FEV1/FVC was 81.8%. 64.6% patients combined with at least one comorbidity. The average diameter of the tumor was 3.28cm. Mean operation time was 181.2 minutes. The post-operative pathology confirmed 59.8% as adenocarcinoma while 30.2% as squamous carcinoma. 88.5%(mean,50% to 100%) patients who were pathologically confirmed as stage III received neo-adjuvant therapy before surgery. The rate of minimally invasive lobectomy surgery was 49.9(mean, 2.31 to 90.2)% in different regions. The number of lymph nodes stations harvested in lobectomy was 5.9(mean, 3.0 to 7.4). Mean hospital cost was 57757 (mean, 42205 to 100113 ) RMB. Conclusions: The heterogeneity of surgical treatment is quite huge in different centers of China. The baseline status before surgery, pre-operative therapy strategy, surgical technique, and health economic data submitted to the registry showed imbalanced development of NSCLC surgical treatment in different regions of China. (Table Presented).
