TY  - JOUR
TI  - Prognostic factors associated with recurrence in early stage node negative lung cancer patients after curative surgical resection-single center experience
AU  - Sunkara, R.
AU  - Schneider, D.
AU  - Rafeq, S.
AU  - Chi, D.
PY  - 2013
AB  - INTRODUCTION: Five year survival in early stage non small cell lung cancer, NSCLC ( Stage IA-IIB) ranges between 38-67% despite curative surgical resection(1). Few retrospective studies in the recent past have attempted to identify the poor prognostic factors affecting survival in these patients. Lymph vascular invasion (LVI) has shown consistently as a marker of recurrence (2). The purpose of the study is to identify prognostic features in early lung cancer patients treated in our institution. METHODS: We reviewed the charts of 150 patients who were diagnosed with early stage lung cancer from 1995 to 2006. Of these, we identified 56 patients who underwent surgery and have available pathology with further follow up at our institution. Kaplan Meier method was used to generate survival curves. Cox proportional hazard model was developed to investigate the association between LVI and recurrence while other clinical factors such as tumor size(>2 vs < 2cm) and resection type were taken into account. RESULTS: The median age is 70 years and median tumor size is 2.0 cm. Thirty patients had lobectomy (L) and 26 had wedge resection (W). Recurrence occurred to 5 (50%) out of the 10 patients with LVI and 11 (26%)out of the 46 patients without LVI. Kaplan-Meier survival curves showed a 5-year recurrence-free rate of 77.1% in patients without LVI compared with 56.2% in those with LVI (Fig. 1, Log rank test p=0.0363). After adjusting the effects of resection and tumor size, LVI still shows significant correlation with recurrence(HR 3.06, p=0.0452) (Table1). CONCLUSION: In early stage, node negative NSCLC patients, LVI remains a poor prognostic factor and is associated with a decreased disease free survival. LVI currently does not influence adjuvant treatment decision in NSCLC. In our study, tumor size and surgery type did not affect the disease recurrence rate. However, our sample size is small to make definitive conclusion. LVI could be considered in the future to guide adjuvant therapy recommendations in early NSCLC.
ID  - 3255
