TY  - JOUR
TI  - Is uniportalthoracoscopic surgerya feasible approach for advanced stages of non-small cell lung cancer?
AU  - Gonzalez-Rivas, D.
AU  - Fieira, E.
AU  - Delgado, M.
AU  - Mendez, L.
AU  - Fernandez, R.
AU  - Paradela, M.
AU  - Garcia, J.
AU  - De La Torre, M.
PY  - 2013
DO  - 10.1093/icvts/ivt288.105
AB  - Objectives: Conventional video-assisted thoracoscopic (VATS) lobectomy for advanced lung cancer is a feasible and safe surgery in experienced centres. The aim of this study is to assess the feasibility of uniportal VATS approach in the treatment of advanced non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) and compare the perioperative outcomes with early-stage tumours. Methods: From June 2010 to December 2012, we performed 163 uniportal VATS major pulmonary resections. Only NSCLC cases were included in this study. Patients were divided in two groups: A, early-stage and B, advanced cases (>5 cm, T3 or T4 tumours, or tumours requiring neoadjuvant treatment). A descriptive, prospective and retrospective study was performed, comparing perioperative outcomes obtained in both groups. Results: A total of 130 cases were included: 87 (A) vs 43 (B) patients (conversion rate 1.1 vs 6.5%, P = 0.119). Mean global age was 64.9 years and 73.6% were man. The patient demographic data were similar in the two groups. Upper lobectomies (A - 56 vs B - 24 patients) and anatomic segmentectomies (4 vs 0) were more frequent in group A while pneumonectomy was more frequent in B (1 vs 6 patients).Surgical time was longer (144.8 ± 41.6 vs 183.2 ± 48.9, P < 0.001), and median number of lymph nodes (14 vs 16, P = 0.004) were statistically higher in group B. Median number of nodal stations (5 vs 5, P = 0.165), days of chest tube (2 vs 2, P = 0.098), hospital stay (3 vs 3, P = 0.072), and rate of complications (18.6 vs 16.3%, P = 0.075) were similar in both groups. A total of 77.4% of patients (A) and 36.6% (B) were classified as stage I after pathological examination. One patient died on the 58th postoperative day in group A. Conclusions: Uniportal VATS lobectomy for advanced cases of NSCLC is a safe and reliable procedure, that provides perioperative outcomes similar to those obtained with early stage tumours. Further analyses of survival for uniportal VATS lobectomy of advanced stage tumours are ongoing.
ID  - 3262
